     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose needs a check first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5,100 mg/day**. The maximum daily dose of metformin is:\n- **2,550 mg/day** for immediate-release (usually 850 mg three times daily)\n- **2,000 mg/day** for extended-release\n\nSo this order is about twice the immediate-release maximum. Even with normal kidney function, that much metformin raises the risk of lactic acidosis and serious stomach and bowel side effects.\n\n**It may have been meant as one of these:**\n1. **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n2. **1700 mg/day split into two doses**, such as 850 mg twice daily\n3. **1000 mg by mouth twice daily** (2,000 mg/day), a common maintenance dose\n\nPlease tell me which dose and frequency you want, and whether it's immediate- or extended-release, and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical reason, and I'll add it as a note on the order. Even then, a pharmacist will probably need to review it."
      }
     ],
