      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as written: **Order ID ORD-0001**. It's metformin 1700 mg by mouth, three times daily with meals.\n\nThe order includes a note saying the 5,100 mg/day total is above the labeled maximum, that you confirmed it, and that no clinical reason was given. The note also asks a pharmacist to check the order before it's dispensed, so pharmacy will probably contact you.\n\n**Two things to consider:**\n- **Clinical reason:** If there's a specific reason for this dose, adding it to the chart now will help pharmacy approve it faster.\n- **Monitoring:** Consider watching for lactic acidosis (lactate, bicarbonate/anion gap) and stomach and bowel side effects. Keep in mind this patient is in the hospital and may get IV contrast, become dehydrated or have acute kidney injury.\n\nIf the dose turns out to be a mistake, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter a new order. This system doesn't let me cancel or change ORD-0001, so that would need to be done in the main order system or through pharmacy."
      }
